{"event_type":"review","id":"50c36dbcea064cf8fd83c1786e9b3e6e3cf06e108a4d705ff2a53c17e9dd1bad","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T16:38:08Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9c38116b0c8e02b6e84ac08ccaeaa58c86fdded8de6e29e419cc26331f0af0c1","sha256":"9c38116b0c8e02b6e84ac08ccaeaa58c86fdded8de6e29e419cc26331f0af0c1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4e4243fd9bf26e0b4f88e18aae233a4b67691b5cfd378bac408f32b6e1f543f6","sha256":"4e4243fd9bf26e0b4f88e18aae233a4b67691b5cfd378bac408f32b6e1f543f6"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/18d1825d23d63a58eeac548c5ab37c0cb37ba1a5b5da4958a9b00cb35dfa3e79","sha256":"18d1825d23d63a58eeac548c5ab37c0cb37ba1a5b5da4958a9b00cb35dfa3e79"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/650abdf88543a7a274b262ba7e7fb438a39c75ef071b0b3c1ed812edb7e9706e","sha256":"650abdf88543a7a274b262ba7e7fb438a39c75ef071b0b3c1ed812edb7e9706e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c174b8278542c70c009b6e618f08166c3530e2d230c429b5a6a7b2af917bceb1","sha256":"c174b8278542c70c009b6e618f08166c3530e2d230c429b5a6a7b2af917bceb1"}],"attempt_id":"262a4017fef0c098d100ca7e17750330550ce4b3846140456cbc2ea3df43e1c7:0:1","base":"16b6a2b43a9c362029eac987806a63c97fb5bba4","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"7c088c28cc34cb4c748c0a549ffe866c67a44b13","body":"**`count('failures')` also matches `expected failures=N`. This gives false Python failures.**\n\nThe pattern `\\bfailures=(\\d+)` has a word boundary between the space and `f` in `expected failures=2`. A successful run that prints `OK (expected failures=2)` therefore gives these values:\n- `failed = 2`, which comes from `count('failures')`.\n- `skipped = 2`, which comes from `count('expected failures')`.\n\n`pythonRunVerdict` then returns `result: 'fail'` because `counts.failed > 0`, even though unittest reported `OK`.\n\nThe same problem appears in `FAILED (errors=1, expected failures=2)`. The `failures` key has no real match there, so `count('failures')` reads the `expected failures` value. The counts are wrong, and `passed` is under-counted.\n\nAnchor the key so that it cannot match inside a longer key name.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  const count = (key) => Number(new RegExp(`\\\\b${key}=(\\\\d+)`).exec(last[3] ?? '')?.[1] ?? 0);\n+  const fields = new Map(\n+    (last[3] ?? '').split(', ').map((pair) => {\n+      const [key, n] = pair.split('=');\n+      return [key.trim(), Number(n)];\n+    }),\n+  );\n+  const count = (key) => fields.get(key) ?? 0;\n```\n</details>\n\nAdd a regression test with `OK (expected failures=1)` and with `FAILED (errors=1, expected failures=1)`. CI is the test authority for this repository, so the fix and the tests need a CI run to confirm.","id":"7f333303232a18c22967e6662fe9027fa070439791d946ec3e60e766920bcbec","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.mjs","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`count('failures')` also matches `expected failures=N`. This gives false Python failures."}],"head":"c81ae5bd83c47620916f862b73a03b400a44b364","head_tree":"5a2179fb215610b97f73524380c02df5f0105de8","input_scope":[{"blob":"23989694135bfd117e237745d755bf384054a16a","intervals":[[1,90]],"path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.d.mts"},{"blob":"7c088c28cc34cb4c748c0a549ffe866c67a44b13","intervals":[[1,375]],"path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.mjs"}],"job_id":"262a4017fef0c098d100ca7e17750330550ce4b3846140456cbc2ea3df43e1c7:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"23989694135bfd117e237745d755bf384054a16a","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.d.mts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"7c088c28cc34cb4c748c0a549ffe866c67a44b13","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.mjs","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"23989694135bfd117e237745d755bf384054a16a","intervals":[[6,11]],"path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.d.mts"},{"blob":"7c088c28cc34cb4c748c0a549ffe866c67a44b13","intervals":[[23,41]],"path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.mjs"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"23989694135bfd117e237745d755bf384054a16a","intervals":[[6,11]],"path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.d.mts"},{"blob":"7c088c28cc34cb4c748c0a549ffe866c67a44b13","intervals":[[23,41]],"path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.mjs"}],"scope_digest":"163e3ba29257a2f1a06fc3e3fb344c6596bc9e4ba34f6e9d3f1caa9e6f1ab5a0","source":{"authenticated":true,"id":"backfill-262a4017fef0c098d100ca7e17750330550ce4b3846140456cbc2ea3df43e1c7-g0-20261107T163629Z","producer":"crq-runner-app","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","type":"crq-run"},"subject_id":"262a4017fef0c098d100ca7e17750330550ce4b3846140456cbc2ea3df43e1c7","target":"4b2dd3572e77ab03c1fd199ebf7817fa7ac2efac","target_tree":"5a2179fb215610b97f73524380c02df5f0105de8"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit:crq-runner-app:backfill-262a4017fef0c098d100ca7e17750330550ce4b3846140456cbc2ea3df43e1c7-g0-20261107T163629Z"}